---
title: 'Pie Series'
description: '$framework Pie Charts display categorical data as proportional slices within a circle. Customise $framework pie chart labels and variable sector radiuses. See API docs for more info.'
---

A Pie Series displays categorical data as proportional slices within a circle.

## Simple Pie

{% chartExampleRunner title="Basic Pie Chart" name="simple-pie" type="generated" /%}

To create a Pie Series, use the `pie` series type.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [{ type: 'pie', angleKey: 'amount', legendItemKey: 'asset' }],
}
```

In this configuration:

- `angleKey` determines the angle of each pie sector. The total of all values will correspond to the full pie.
- `legendItemKey` configures the names to be used in the legend for each sector.

## Labels

The Pie Series supports two types of label related to individual sectors.

- Callout labels are displayed adjacent to each sector, connected with callout line.
- Sector labels are displayed inside each sector.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Pie Chart with Labels" name="pie-labels" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'pie',
            angleKey: 'amount',
            calloutLabelKey: 'asset',
            sectorLabelKey: 'amount',
            sectorLabel: {
                color: 'white',
                fontWeight: 'bold',
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

In this configuration:

- `calloutLabelKey` defines the variable used for the callout labels. This is also used in the [Legend](./legend/) if no `legendItemKey` is provided, and in the [Tooltips](./tooltips/).
- `sectorLabelKey` defines the variable used for the sector labels.

By default, callout labels won't be displayed for sectors with a value of `0`. Set `calloutLabel.minAngle = 0` to show these.

It is possible to customise the text displayed in these labels by using the `calloutLabel.formatter` and `sectorLabel.formatter`.
These functions receive a single object as a parameter containing the options and datum associated with a pie sector, and should return a string.

Please see the [API reference](#api-reference) for options to customise `calloutLabel`, `calloutLine` and `sectorLabel`, as well as other series customisations.

### Label Fitting

Both label types can be constrained to the space available rather than overflowing or being dropped. Sector labels are fitted to the wedge they sit in, and callout labels to the bounds given by `maxWidth` and `maxHeight`.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Pie Chart with Fitted Labels" name="label-fitting" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'pie',
            angleKey: 'terawattHours',
            calloutLabelKey: 'source',
            sectorLabelKey: 'share',
            calloutLabel: {
                maxWidth: 70,
                wrapping: 'on-space',
                truncate: true,
            },
            sectorLabel: {
                wrapping: 'on-space',
                truncate: true,
                minimumFontSize: 8,
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

In this example:

- `maxWidth` and `maxHeight` cap the label size in pixels. A sector label is capped by its wedge as well, and whichever bound is tighter applies.
- `wrapping` (`'on-space'`, `'always'`, `'hyphenate'`, `'never'`) controls how overflowing text wraps within those bounds.
- `truncate` appends an ellipsis to whatever still does not fit. With it disabled the label is hidden instead.
- `minimumFontSize` lets the label shrink to fit before it is truncated or hidden. Switch it on to see cut-short labels render in full at a smaller size.

The Donut Series supports the same options, as shown by the Series control in the example above. See [Series Labels](./series-labels/#collision-avoidance) for how these options behave across other series types.

## Variable Sector Radius

It is possible to visualise a second variable in the Pie Series by using the `radiusKey` to vary the radius of a sector based on the values. This is also known as a **Rose Chart**.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Sectors with Different Radii" name="sector-radius" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'pie',
            radiusKey: 'yield',
            angleKey: 'amount',
            legendItemKey: 'asset',
        },
    ],
}
```

